.TH DCC-KBD-DAEMON 8 2026-11-27 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-kbd-daemon \- keyboard backlight daemon of Dudes Control Center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-kbd-daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-kbd-daemon
runs as root from
.BR dcc-kbd-daemon.service .
It drives the per-key RGB LEDs
.I rgb:kbd_backlight*
in
.I /sys/class/leds
that the
.B ite_829x
kernel module provides, and keyboard backlights of other laptops through
the kernel's standard LED class:
.TP
.B per-key
16 or more multicolor LEDs (ite_829x): profiles, zones and effects per key.
.TP
.B rgb
1 to 15 multicolor LEDs with
.I multi_intensity
(one color, or a few zones that all get the same color); the color order
comes from
.IR multi_index .
.TP
.B white
a single-color LED
.I *::kbd_backlight
(for example thinkpad_acpi, dell\-laptop): only on/off and brightness.
Off sets the brightness to 0 and keeps the level for switching on.
.PP
STATUS reports the kind as
.B KBD_TYPE=per\-key|rgb|white|none
and the kernel driver as
.BR KBD_DRIVER= .
Without any keyboard backlight the daemon keeps running and looks again
every 10 seconds, so a driver loaded later is found.
.PP
A keyboard profile has a base color for all keys and any number of named
zones, each with its own color and set of keys.
A profile without a base color and without zones leaves the keyboard dark.
.PP
The base color and each zone can have an animated effect: Breathing (the
color fades in and out), Rainbow (all its keys cycle through the colors) or
Wave (a rainbow runs across the keyboard to the right, left, down or up),
each with a speed from 1 to 10.
The daemon draws them up to 20 times per second and writes only keys whose
color changed; a full-keyboard frame is limited by the keyboard controller
(one USB request per key).
Effects pause while the backlight or its brightness is off.
Profiles are stored in the
.B keyboard_profiles
section of the desktop user's
.I profiles.json
(see
.BR dudes-control-center (7)).
On start the daemon lights the active profile, unless the backlight was
switched off.
.PP
Clients connect to
.IR /run/dcc-kbd.sock ;
only root and members of the group
.B dudes-control-center
are accepted.
.BR dcc-gui (1)
and
.BR dcc-kbd-cli (1)
use it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dcc-kbd.sock
Command socket.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dudes-control-center/kbd_backlight_off
Exists while the backlight is switched off; kept across reboots.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dudes-control-center/kbd_brightness
Last hardware brightness.
.TP
.I /var/log/dudes-control-center/KBD_BACKLIGHT_DAEMON.log
Log (rotated at 1 MB, 5 old files kept).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/dcc-kbd-daemon.service
Service; it does not start while
.I /etc/dudes-control-center/disabled-keyboard
exists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DCC_PROFILES_PATH
Absolute path of the
.I profiles.json
to use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-kbd-cli (1),
.BR dcc-gui (1),
.BR dcc-component (8)
